meta {
  name: Stream all events
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/events/workflows
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: text/event-stream
}

docs {
  Server-Sent Events stream of every WorkflowEvent emitted by the daemon.

  Event types (each delivered as `data: <json>` over SSE):
  - `RunStarted` — { run_id, workflow_id, workflow_version, started_at }
  - `StepStarted` — { run_id, workflow_id, step_index, step_id, kind, started_at }
  - `StepOutput` — { run_id, workflow_id, step_index, step_id, data, finished_at } (chunk of stdout/stderr)
  - `StepCompleted` — { run_id, workflow_id, step_index, step_id, status, exit_code, cost_usd, finished_at }
  - `RunCompleted` — { run_id, workflow_id, status, total_duration_ms, total_cost_usd, finished_at }
  - `RunFailed` — { run_id, workflow_id, error, finished_at }
  - `WorkflowChanged` — { workflow_id, kind } (Created / Updated / Deleted / Enabled / Disabled)

  Bruno's HTTP runner displays incoming SSE events live. Open this request,
  hit Send, then trigger a workflow in another tab — you'll see the run
  unfold in real time.
}
